[1879383038]={[1]="Winterstith Gloves of the Warrior";[2]="‘Thirteen kings, you say? Ah, it is an ill-omened number. How many more dwarves will die in sight of the Anvil before the dragons are swept away?’ – Kópat of the Zhélruka";[3]=5;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB963;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383039]={[1]="Winterstith Trousers of Finesse";[2]="‘Karazgar has not been seen for more than ten years. I think he is dead.’ - Bótuz Frostblood";[3]=15;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411AEFD4;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383041]={[1]="Reinforced Winterstith Boots of Fortitude";[2]="‘Let the Óinsbridge be a reminder to us that our actions will remain, even once we are gone! These dragons cannot best us!’ - King Óin’s son Dáin, shortly before he disappeared in the Ered Mithrin";[3]=23;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB965;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383042]={[1]="Anvil-forged Chestplate of the Defender";[2]="Borin embraced his nephew, and followed the rest of his people. Turning back, he saw Frór standing beneath the dragon, his sword drawn. Vethúg wheeled in the air and began to dive.";[3]=3;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB95C;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383045]={[1]="Reinforced Winterstith Leggings of the Warrior";[2]="Ingór charged the dragon, his sword held high, but he never landed a blow. Hrímil Frost-heart swallowed him entire: sword, armour, and all. Only the memory of that mighty warrior remains.";[3]=15;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411AEFD4;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383046]={[1]="Anvil-forged Sabatons of Fortitude";[2]="‘Build the new bridge with stones of the mountains, and it will outlast any storm,’ King Óin commanded, and it was done. It stands to this day.";[3]=23;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB962;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383047]={[1]="Winterstith Mantle of Precision";[2]="During the reign of Rúrek the Slaughterer, dwarves slew dozens of drakes throughout Ered Mithrin, but at the cost of many more Zhélruka lives. ‘It is a fair exchange,’ Rúrek is reported to have said.";[3]=6;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB94B;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383049]={[1]="Reinforced Winterstith Boots of Concentration";[2]="‘What do I know of Brátek the Brash? I know he was a master of strategy and tactics, and won a number of victories against the Witch-king himself! I know too that it was not enough: the stealthy blade of Karazgar proved his undoing.’ - Khîl Tale-spinner";[3]=23;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB965;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383050]={[1]="Winterstith Mantle of Charity";[2]="The dragons lay sleeping in their hiding-places for hundreds of years, unremembered by their foes, but when they awoke they had not forgotten their ancient hatreds. So began the War of Dwarves and Dragons.";[3]=6;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB94B;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383051]={[1]="Anvil-forged Gauntlets of Fortitude";[2]="‘Build the new bridge with stones of the mountains, and it will outlast any storm,’ King Óin commanded, and it was done. It stands to this day.";[3]=5;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB930;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383052]={[1]="Reinforced Winterstith Boots of the Defender";[2]="Vethúg concealed herself in a high cavern behind a mighty waterfall near the Steel Keep, and waited. As Dáin raised his axe before his cheering people, she burst from her cave, the waterfall freezing and shattering into shards around her, and swept down upon the Longbeards.";[3]=23;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB965;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383053]={[1]="Winterstith Shoes of Concentration";[2]="‘I find the more I gaze upon the smooth ice of the Anvil the more reluctant I am to leave it behind, as if it carries upon its surface some strange power of bewitchment! Do you feel it too?’ - Durin, son of Thorin Stonehelm";[3]=23;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB95D;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383058]={[1]="Anvil-forged Gauntlets of Reflexes";[2]="‘The worms of Ered Mithrin grow to tremendous size, it is true, but what will really take you by surprise is their great speed. The cursed things are fast! Or so I’m told.’ - Khîl Tale-spinner";[3]=5;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB930;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383059]={[1]="Reinforced Winterstith Boots of Reflexes";[2]="‘Dragons, Orcs, worms… I fear none of these beasts. Let them fear me!’ – King Dóbruz II, devoured by trolls while seeking lost Thafar-gathol";[3]=23;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB965;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383060]={[1]="Reinforced Winterstith Leggings of Finesse";[2]="‘King Kámluz moved the throne to the Steel Keep, claiming he sought to mine the iron and silver of the Ered Mithrin. But it was not so! He desired the mithril of lost Thafar-gathol.’ - Khîl Tale-spinner";[3]=15;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411AEFD4;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383061]={[1]="Reinforced Winterstith Gages of Precision";[2]="In time, Rúrek V came to be known as Rúrek the Slaughterer, and during his reign the Zhélruka waged war upon dragonkind; but it was an imprecise war, and the dragons that would prove most dangerous to them survived.";[3]=5;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB950;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383062]={[1]="Anvil-forged Gauntlets of the Defender";[2]="Borin embraced his nephew, and followed the rest of his people. Turning back, he saw Frór standing beneath the dragon, his sword drawn. Vethúg wheeled in the air and began to dive.";[3]=5;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB930;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383064]={[1]="Reinforced Winterstith Hauberk of Precision";[2]="In time, Rúrek V came to be known as Rúrek the Slaughterer, and during his reign the Zhélruka waged war upon dragonkind; but it was an imprecise war, and the dragons that would prove most dangerous to them survived.";[3]=3;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB967;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383065]={[1]="Anvil-forged Helm of Finesse";[2]="‘There is more to victory in combat than brute strength,’ King Kámluz told his people. He proved himself right, dying before the Anvil in the jaws of a cold-drake.";[3]=7;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB939;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383066]={[1]="Anvil-forged Helm of Alacrity";[2]="Countless dwarves set forth from Thikil-gundu and other lesser keeps in Ered Mithrin, eager to discover lost Thafar-gathol and seize its riches for their own. This eagerness proved their undoing.";[3]=7;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB939;[9]=0x41000004;};
