[1879383192]={[1]="Winterstith Cap of Fortitude";[2]="King Ilkún's search lasted for ten years, but ended in horror. While digging beneath the Anvil, the Zhélruka caused a great crack to split the glacier in twain. The cold-drakes who dwelt within Winterstith awoke and emerged from the rent, overwhelming the dwarves.";[3]=7;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB953;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383194]={[1]="Winterstith Gloves of Precision";[2]="During the reign of Rúrek the Slaughterer, dwarves slew dozens of drakes throughout Ered Mithrin, but at the cost of many more Zhélruka lives. ‘It is a fair exchange,’ Rúrek is reported to have said.";[3]=5;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB963;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383196]={[1]="Reinforced Winterstith Boots of Alacrity";[2]="‘Longbeards hurry to battle. We Zhélruka must exercise restraint, if we can. Victory comes more slowly than defeat; treasure one and not the other.’ - Brátek IV, the Brash";[3]=23;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB965;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383201]={[1]="Winterstith Mantle of the Warrior";[2]="‘Thirteen kings, you say? Ah, it is an ill-omened number. How many more dwarves will die in sight of the Anvil before the dragons are swept away?’ – Kópat of the Zhélruka";[3]=6;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB94B;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383203]={[1]="Anvil-forged Greaves of Reflexes";[2]="‘The worms of Ered Mithrin grow to tremendous size, it is true, but what will really take you by surprise is their great speed. The cursed things are fast! Or so I’m told.’ - Khîl Tale-spinner";[3]=15;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411AEFD4;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383205]={[1]="Winterstith Gloves of Concentration";[2]="‘I find the more I gaze upon the smooth ice of the Anvil the more reluctant I am to leave it behind, as if it carries upon its surface some strange power of bewitchment! Do you feel it too?’ - Durin, son of Thorin Stonehelm";[3]=5;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB963;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383207]={[1]="Reinforced Winterstith Boots of Precision";[2]="In time, Rúrek V came to be known as Rúrek the Slaughterer, and during his reign the Zhélruka waged war upon dragonkind; but it was an imprecise war, and the dragons that would prove most dangerous to them survived.";[3]=23;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB965;[9]=0x41000004;};
[1879383213]={[1]="Reinforced Winterstith Gages of Fortitude";[2]="‘Let the Óinsbridge be a reminder to us that our actions will remain, even once we are gone! These dragons cannot best us!’ - King Óin’s son Dáin, shortly before he disappeared in the Ered Mithrin";[3]=5;[4]=3;[5]=3;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x411CB950;[9]=0x41000004;};
