[1879395499]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="They blazed as bright as stars, crimson and sapphire, and he too shone, silver-white. This, then, was the unveiled wrath of the Eldar, not seen in Middle-earth since the Elder days.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395500]={[1]="Rune-inscribed Page";[2]="I have forsaken my name. It matters not, for I am named anew. I am Agath-kali, Shadow-woman, Mistress of Lamentation. And still I serve the Eye.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395501]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="He took those dread jewels and, standing on the stony hilltop above the plain’s foul reek, slipped them on his fingers, each to one hand.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395502]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="Long had we been friends, and many battles had I fought beside him, but not until the fall of the Black Gate did I behold Gil-galad’s true might.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395503]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="'Yet to don both,' Elrond said. 'Never did even the mightiest of the Gwaith-i-Mírdain dare to wear two!' But Gil-galad's mind was set, and he would not be swayed.'";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395504]={[1]="Rune-inscribed Page";[2]="As reward, I was blessed to be the first to bleed there. I gave myself freely, gladly. I sang as I writhed in my throes before the Dark Tree.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395505]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="'Rightly so,' said Círdan. 'For the Enemy will see.' The Elvenking nodded. 'Still, what other choice remains? How many more of our people must die because of my doubt?'";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395506]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="Through smoke and blood we pressed, but against Mordor’s gates even the Great Alliance broke like waves upon the strand.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395507]={[1]="Rune-inscribed Page";[2]="Even as I perished, I felt the Black Breath upon me. It held shut death’s gates, unmade and made me again, in likeness to the Gaunt Ones of old.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395508]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="'Celebrimbor vouchsafed them to me ere his death, then I to those I trusted, for I feared that I might be tempted to use them.'";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395509]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="It was upon the battle-plain of Dagorlad, where for months we had spent our blood against the Enemy, that at last I understood the Elven-king’s power.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395510]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="'These,' Gil-galad said, 'are Vilya and Narya, two of the three Great Rings saved from Sauron’s vengeance when he brought Eregion to ruin.'";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395511]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="A shadow fell upon Gil-galad’s brow as we met that morn, above fields sown with the dead, and gazed upon that grim bastion.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395512]={[1]="Glowing Page";[2]="Those who defiled it are slain, or else driven back to Mordor. The banners of Sauron darken its parapets no more.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395513]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="Though we long strove, besting even the Dark Lord’s mightiest servants, those fell ramparts yielded not. Surely the halls of Barad-dûr rang with Sauron’s laughter at our despair.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395514]={[1]="Rune-inscribed Page";[2]="When Eärnur, that vainglorious fool, rode to the Dead City to challenge the Captain, I did not yet fathom the weaving of our fates.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395515]={[1]="Glowing Page";[2]="Some of the evils visited upon this place cannot be undone. The White Tree, scion of Telperion, we found hewn and burnt.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395516]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="'Since first we rode to war, I have dreaded this day.' We Men who stood with him did not yet understand, but Gil-galad’s captains knew, and they sorrowed.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395517]={[1]="Glowing Page";[2]="Thy beloved libraries are plundered, and much wisdom forever lost. Not all harms can be healed, yet much of worth can still be saved, should those with power will it.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395518]={[1]="Rune-inscribed Page";[2]="I serve the Eye, but only of late did I know my place in his designs. A priestess I was then, my knives red from work in his name.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395519]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="Never in all our days together had I seen him in a mood so grim. 'It has come to this, then,' he said, leaning upon Aeglos his spear.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395520]={[1]="Rune-inscribed Page";[2]="When the Nine claimed Minas Ithil, I was there. I marched through its riven gates. I watched its towers darken, heard its people’s cries of anguish. Such music.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395521]={[1]="Glowing Page";[2]="My lady, I fear thy husband is of harsher mind. When he saw the Moon-tower so afflicted, he deemed it must be razed rather than allowed to linger.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395522]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="Each bore in his hand a golden ring – the Lord of Imladris’ set with a gem of deepest blue; the Shipwright’s with a stone of flaming red.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395523]={[1]="Glowing Page";[2]="He loathes what Minas Ithil has become, and believes it forever tainted. When I claimed otherwise he grew grim and would not be moved.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395524]={[1]="Rune-inscribed Page";[2]="I serve the Eye, though never have I beheld the Dark Lord. His day is yet far off, but that is well. There is much yet to do.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395525]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="They sought to discourage him, but he would not be daunted, and so, though it pained them, Elrond and Círdan both came forward.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395526]={[1]="Glowing Page";[2]="Oft it is the way of men to destroy that which no longer pleases them, rather than taking the care to mend it.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395527]={[1]="Ancient Page";[2]="My lady, I fear the mother of this plague to be Ungwetári, that most loathsome of Ungoliant’s brood that troubled our kindred in Beleriand.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395528]={[1]="Rune-inscribed Page";[2]="I have forsaken my name. It matters not. The frail thing I was is best forgotten – a cage of flesh and blood. I have moved beyond it.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395529]={[1]="Ancient Page";[2]="Should my fears prove true I will need aid against her, for I am loth to lead my Company to slaughter as I did in the disaster of Udûn.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395530]={[1]="Glowing Page";[2]="Yet it is my hope that some fondness for this vale endures in thee. Mayhap thy words might cause Isildur’s heart to yield.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395531]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="The battlements, which had for so long withstood all our cunning and strength, rent asunder with a roar, and were flung to the earth as splinters and dust.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395532]={[1]="Ancient Page";[2]="Two nights ago we hazarded to stalk her beneath the moonless sky, but when we sprang upon her our blades would not pierce her hide.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395533]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="Terror and awe filled my heart as the storm fell upon the haunted pass, hurling our foes like children’s toys, and at last smote the black gates themselves.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395534]={[1]="Glowing Page";[2]="In return, this is my vow: that the Galadhrim will tarry in Ithilien. For while growing things endure, with care we can wash the Enemy’s foulness from the land.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395535]={[1]="Ancient Page";[2]="Being sly she caught us, and would have feasted upon our bones, but by chance the cloud-wrack rent and the stars were unveiled.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395536]={[1]="Glowing Page";[2]="More, I will bestow virtues, known to the Noldor, upon the city. Its stones shall shine with the Moon’s light, caught and held by the craft of my kin.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395537]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="At his beckoning, the storm came – a vast column of fire and rushing wind that fell like a hammer from the wrack above.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395538]={[1]="Glowing Page";[2]="Our Enemy is cruel, and his throngs know naught of mercy. Still have I seen the courage of my people and thine proven many times.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395539]={[1]="Ancient Page";[2]="When the light of Eärendil shone upon her she quailed and fled back to the gloom of her caves, as if the glimmer itself hurt her.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395540]={[1]="Glowing Page";[2]="In this way it shall be a Gondolin renewed: a beacon against night, under thy care, and that of thy daughters after thee.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395541]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="A silence fell upon the Dagorlad as Gil-galad raised his hands and spoke words of power: 'Lachalagos dan in ennyn vyrn!'";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395542]={[1]="Glowing Page";[2]="Thy husband Isildur fought alongside mine own before the gates of Minas Anor. Should we defeat the Shadow, minstrels shall long sing of their valour.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395543]={[1]="Ancient Page";[2]="This, I deem, is our best hope. For while slaying her may lie beyond our power, still we may hem her in.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395544]={[1]="Glowing Page";[2]="We have come at last to the lands whence Sauron's servants drove thee. Long have the Elves esteemed the Ithil-vale, for we walked here in the Elder Days.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395545]={[1]="Ancient Page";[2]="Once, when first we were betrothed, you lit the caverns of Doriath with Star-glasses, filled with Eärendil's glow, the Gilgelair of song.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395546]={[1]="Glowing Page";[2]="So much did we love the moonrise there that when first I heard that Isildur had bidden a city built therein, I grieved that the vale had been sullied.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395547]={[1]="Ancient Page";[2]="It would take but a few such glasses, cunningly ensconced within her caverns, to keep Ungwetári penned and stay her offspring from befouling the land.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395548]={[1]="Rune-inscribed Page";[2]="The labours that followed were hard, their fruit disappointing. A King’s screams, it happens, sound little different from any other man’s.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395549]={[1]="Ancient Page";[2]="While I await your reply we will battle on against the scourge of Torech Ungol, but the sullying of the vale cannot be stemmed forever.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395550]={[1]="Rune-inscribed Page";[2]="'If we wished him dead, he would die,' they whispered. 'A task awaits, one he alone can accomplish. You will compel him. Use all your skill.'";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395551]={[1]="Ancient Page";[2]="I beseech you to send help with speed, that I might sooner return home and know once more the bliss of your touch. I remain your beloved, Celeborn";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395552]={[1]="Rune-inscribed Page";[2]="Never would I have dreamed of such an honour. Less still what was to come. For I was not to kill him; death was not their aim.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395553]={[1]="Glowing Page";[2]="My lady Valardis: in time of darkness and doubt, I send thee tidings of hope. The war wears on all, and many battles yet lie ahead.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395554]={[1]="Rune-inscribed Page";[2]="After they took him, the Nazgûl gave him to me. To me! The King of Gondor … its last, if the whispers were true.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395555]={[1]="Ancient Page";[2]="That it lies on the threshold of the Shadowed Land cannot be mere accident. Dark forces are moving, and though Morgoth’s domain is ended, his servants abide still.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395556]={[1]="Ancient Page";[2]="As you beheld in your mirror ere my company rode forth, a stain attaints Imlad Ithil, a shadow among the mountains that darkens the valley below.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395557]={[1]="Ancient Page";[2]="Powers of night yet linger in this world, and one such lies near. Thus I send this message; may the blessings of the Valar guide it into your hands.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395558]={[1]="Glowing Page";[2]="I say now that I was wrong to sorrow. I have beheld Minas Ithil, and it wakes in my heart an ache I had thought never again to feel.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395559]={[1]="Ancient Page";[2]="Even to share the grace of your thoughts would be a balm to me, but I dare no such risk.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395560]={[1]="Glowing Page";[2]="I knew Gondolin of old, and while no city of Elves or Men can equal its splendour, thy stronghold is as like to it as any could now build.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395561]={[1]="Ancient Page";[2]="Galadriel, elanor nîn, I sorrow to be parted from you, and long to feel again your embrace in the star-lit gardens of Eregion our home.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395562]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="'But that he guesses not. It may help us before the end.' The foe fled before us, and we marched to the last great siege.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395563]={[1]="Glowing Page";[2]="I wept to see it Orc-befouled. I have watched many lands fall into ruin and decay. When I saw Ithilien, I knew my part in this war was its rescue.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395564]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="'And what will you do?' asked Círdan. Gil-galad sighed and shook his head. 'Naught, save at fearful need. I doubt I should survive it a second time.'";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395565]={[1]="Glowing Page";[2]="Now I say to thee: rejoice, for thy city is freed. With what power we wield, Celeborn and I have taken back Minas Ithil.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395566]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="Gil-galad nodded, then grew stern again. 'But so, too, did he behold mine. And though Sauron’s own Ring is powerful, he now fears what I might do with mine.'";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395567]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="His light dimmed, and to my eyes he seemed wearier than ever I had seen him before. 'What did you see?' Elrond asked. 'Did you behold his mind?'";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395568]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="He sank to his knees, and Elrond and Círdan at once took hold of him. His strength spent, he let them wrest the Rings from his hands.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395569]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="So, at last, was the Land of Shadows laid bare – but Gil-galad’s eyes filled not with triumph but with anguish.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395570]={[1]="Ancient Page";[2]="My fellows and I toil to scour the land of them, but always more come to take their place. One might more easily drain the Sea with a ewer.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395571]={[1]="Rune-inscribed Page";[2]="In the end, though, he did what the Nazgûl bade. When I was finished, he had become Mordirith … only a husk of despair, a wretched thing. But it sufficed.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395572]={[1]="Ancient Page";[2]="It lurks in the darkness, coming forth to hunt only in darkest night, but its spawn swarm over the mountains, a fell, crawling pestilence.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395573]={[1]="Ancient Page";[2]="Now I know that one, at least, escaped. The fiend that bedevils the Vale of the Moon has a spider’s likeness, though far more terrible.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395574]={[1]="Rune-inscribed Page";[2]="They turned him loose; not to return to Gondor, for he was too ruined even to want that any longer, but to flee into the mountains.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395575]={[1]="Ancient Page";[2]="When I and the Bright Company battled the children of Ungoliant in the Ered Mithrin at the dawn of this age, I thought we had slain them all.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395576]={[1]="Rune-inscribed Page";[2]="I watched the Nazgûl befoul that Tree, reveled in the King’s sobs as I beheld what their sorcery made of it: Morloth the Black, the Dire, the Profane.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395577]={[1]="Rune-inscribed Page";[2]="In our master’s honour we built this fane, this Woeful House where I have ever after worked my craft. A shrine of pain, of tears, of mingled death and life.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395578]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="And this thought now haunts my dreams: if the Elf-rings hold such power, what strength might dwell within that of the Dark Lord himself?";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395579]={[1]="Rune-inscribed Page";[2]="The Nine knew what he would find. They knew a King’s uses. For two thousand years the White Tree had grown in that hidden vale, beyond the ken of Men.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395580]={[1]="Stark-white Page";[2]="Gil-galad nevermore spoke of that day, nor did any behold his full power again. But since, his words have burned in my mind – Sauron’s own Ring.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395581]={[1]="Rune-inscribed Page";[2]="He sniffed it out like a hound. When he saw the Nine had followed him, he clawed its bark, as if he might tear it down with his bloody fingers.";[3]=27;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x4100319B;[9]=0x410002A9;};
[1879395607]={[1]="Copy of Lost Lore: Thuringwath";[2]="The tale of Mordirith and Morloth.";[3]=205;[4]=2;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x41003199;[9]=0x41000003;};
[1879395608]={[1]="Copy of Lost Lore: Minas Morgul";[2]="A promise from the Lady of Lórien";[3]=205;[4]=2;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x41003199;[9]=0x41000003;};
[1879395609]={[1]="Copy of Lost Lore: Cirith Ungol";[2]="A letter to Galadriel regarding the finding of Ungwetári.";[3]=205;[4]=2;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x41003199;[9]=0x41000003;};
[1879395619]={[1]="Sinister Wing";[2]="A trophy gathered from a corpse. Trophies can be sold to vendors for coin. This item can be collected into task carry-alls. This item may be turned in for tasks in the Wells of Langflood and in Azanulbizar.";[3]=207;[4]=5;[5]=0;[6]=false;[7]=false;[8]=0x410084F2;[9]=0x410030C4;};
